# data/bitext/Bitext_Sample_Customer_Support_Training_Dataset_27K_responses-v11.csv
# data/bitext/cleaned_bitext_training_data.csv
# Keep: data/twcs/sample.csv, data/bitext/data_desc.md, and models/ artifacts
# Keep (IMPORTANT): data/twcs/llm_labeled_5k.csv -- not regenerable, it is many
# sessions of LLM labeling, not the output of a script.
data/twcs/sample_pool_5000.txt
#
# llm_labeled_out_of_sample.csv (ignored at the top of this file) is the same
# kind of artifact -- 639 threads labeled before the random sample existed --
# and is equally unreproducible, but it is deliberately untracked: it is not
# part of the uniform sample and must not be mixed into base-rate or evaluation
# figures. Back it up outside the repo.

# Fine-tuned DistilBERT weights (~256 MB each, regenerable by notebooks 03 and 04).
# The metrics JSON now lives inside these folders for symmetry with models/*/tfidf/,
# so it must be re-included below -- it is the tracked deliverable, and it is what the
# notebooks read for their comparison tables.
# Written as `dir/*` rather than `dir/` so the metrics file can be re-included: an
# ignored *directory* cannot have its contents re-included, an ignored glob can.
models/bitext/distilbert/*
models/twcs/distilbert/*
!models/bitext/distilbert/*_metrics.json
!models/twcs/distilbert/*_metrics.json
!models/twcs/distilbert/casing_ablation.json

# src/ scripts — logic lives in the notebooks; standalone scripts are redundant.
# Written as `src/*` rather than `src/` so a single file can be re-included below:
# an ignored *directory* cannot have its contents re-included, an ignored glob can.
src/*

# Exception: the notebooks import this module at run time, so it has to ship with
# them or the deliverable notebooks cannot be executed from a fresh clone.
!src/distilbert_utils.py
